<description>
Move the grey divider to the far edge of the left-hand mirror slot and recolor matching red markers blue.

Input structure
- The grid has a black background and one full-height grey vertical divider.
- Blue marker pixels are to the left of the divider; red marker pixels are to the right.

Rule
- Let the divider be at column k; erase it and draw it at column 2*k+1.
- Reflect the horizontal span of the left blue markers across the original divider.
- If red markers between the old and new divider occupy exactly that reflected column span, recolor those red pixels blue.

Key insight
- The new divider creates a mirror slot with the same width as the left partition; only the red mask whose column span matches the reflected blue span is converted.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_to_match",
  "src": "blue marker mask s left of the full-height grey divider",
  "dst": "red marker mask d in the mirror slot between the old and shifted divider",
  "match_cond": "d.column_span == reflection of s.column_span across the old divider",
  "transform": "move the grey divider from column k to column 2*k+1; recolor matched d from red to blue and preserve all other markers"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 7x15 [observed]
  background: BLACK
  colors: BLACK, BLUE, GREY, RED only
  divider:
    type: full-height grey vertical line (1 column, all rows grey)
    input_col: 1-5 (call it k); constraint 2k+1 < W
    output_col: 2k+1 (divider erased at k, redrawn at 2k+1)
  left_partition: cols 0..k-1, contains only BLACK and BLUE pixels
  blue_markers:
    count: 1-5 scattered single pixels in left partition
    col_span: contiguous or gapped; min_col always 0 [observed]
  mirror_slot: cols k+1..2k (width = k), contains only BLACK and RED pixels
  beyond_slot: cols 2k+2..W-1, contains only BLACK and RED; always >=2 red pixels
  mirror_slot_red:
    cols are contiguous when present; may be empty (0-7 pixels)
  match_condition: |
    Reflect blue col span across col k: reflected = [2k - max_blue_col, 2k - min_blue_col].
    If mirror-slot red col span == reflected span exactly, recolor those red->blue.
    Otherwise output keeps all red unchanged. ~60% of examples match [observed].
  new_sep_col: col 2k+1 must be BLACK in input (no red/blue there)

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction
  steps:
    1. Pick grid 7x15, choose k in 1-5 ensuring 2k+1 < 15.
    2. Place grey divider at col k.
    3. Scatter 1-5 blue pixels in cols 0..k-1 (at most 1-2 per row).
    4. Compute reflected span [2k - max_bc, 2k - min_bc].
    5. With ~60% probability, place red pixels in mirror slot spanning exactly
       the reflected columns (1+ red pixels per reflected col, contiguous cols).
       Otherwise place 0-2 red cols in mirror slot that do NOT match reflected span.
    6. Ensure col 2k+1 is empty (no markers).
    7. Scatter 2-12 red pixels in cols 2k+2..14 (avoiding adjacency clustering).
```
</generation_spec>
